"Part 2 of 2 (VMMaker.oscog-cb.3823): a 40-byte AbstractInstruction (was 64 bytes on 64-bit platforms).
 Builds on Part 1 (VMMaker.oscog-cb.3822), which introduced the machineCodeBuffer and address accessors.
 - The address is held as a 32-bit offset from codeBase (inst var renamed to addressOffset).
 - operands (still full width) and machineCode share storage in an anonymous union.
 - Since concretization reads operands while writing machine code, machine code is generated into a
   scratch buffer (concretizationScratch) and copied into the union by concretizeAt:.
 - dependent and the operands are unchanged.  Touches only CogAbstractInstruction and Cogit."!

VMStructType subclass: #CogAbstractInstruction
	instanceVariableNames: 'opcode machineCodeSize maxSize annotation machineCode operands addressOffset dependent cogit objectMemory bcpc'
	classVariableNames: 'NumOperands'
	poolDictionaries: 'CogAbstractRegisters CogCompilationConstants CogRTLOpcodes'
	category: 'VMMaker-JIT'!
!CogAbstractInstruction commentStamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30' prior: 0!
I am an abstract instruction generated by the Cogit.  I am subsequently concretized to machine code for the current processor.  A sequence of concretized CogAbstractInstructions are concatenated to form the code for a CogMethod.  I am an abstract class.  My concrete subclasses concretize to the machine code of a specific processor.

In C an AbstractInstruction is a 40 byte struct on 64-bit platforms:
	opcode, machineCodeSize, maxSize, annotation	4 bytes
	addressOffset	the address as a 32-bit offset from the code zone's base (see address & address:)
	dependent		a pointer to the dependent instruction, if any
	union { operands[3]; machineCode[...] }	24 bytes
The operands and the machine code share storage; their lifetimes are disjoint: operands are written when the instruction is generated and read until it is concretized, and machine code is written when concretizing and read when outputting.  Since concretizing reads the operands while it generates machine code, the machine code is generated into a separate buffer and copied into machineCode afterwards (see machineCodeBuffer & concretizeAt:).  The operands of an instruction are therefore not available once it has been concretized (except for instructions that generate no code, such as labels).  In Smalltalk addressOffset holds the address itself, and operands and machineCode are separate arrays.

Instance Variables
	addressOffset:		<Integer>
	bcpc:				<Integer>
	cogit:				<Cogit>
	dependent:			<AbstractInstruction|nil>
	machineCode:		<CArray on: (ByteArray|Array)>
	machineCodeSize:	<Integer>
	maxSize:			<Integer>
	objectMemory:		<NewCoObjectMemory|SpurCoMemoryManager etc>
	opcode:			<Integer>
	operands:			<CArray on: Array>

addressOffset
	- the address at which the instruction will be generated; in C an offset from the code zone's base (see Cogit>>codeOffsetForAddress:)

bcpc
	- the bytecode pc for which the instruction was generated; simulation only

cogit
	- the Cogit assembling the receiver; simulation only

dependent
	- a reference to another instruction which depends on the receiver, if any; in C this is a pointer

machineCode
	- the array of machine code the receiver generates when concretized

machineCodeSize
	- the size of machineCode in bytes

maxSize
	- the maximum size of machine code that the current instruction will generate, in bytes

objectMemory
	- the memory manager for the system; simulation only

opcode
	- the opcode for the receiver which defines which abstract opcode it represents; see CogRTLOpcodes class>>initialize and CogAbstractInstruction subclass initialize methods

operands
	- the array containing any operands the instruction may have; the opcode defines implicitly how many operands are consdered!

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
address
	"In C the address is held as a 32-bit offset from the code zone's base; see Cogit>>codeAddressForOffset:"
	<inline: true>
	<returnTypeC: #usqInt>
	^self cCode: [cogit codeAddressForOffset: addressOffset] inSmalltalk: [addressOffset]! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
address: theAddress
	"In C the address is held as a 32-bit offset from the code zone's base; see Cogit>>codeOffsetForAddress:"
	<inline: true>
	addressOffset := self cCode: [cogit codeOffsetForAddress: theAddress] inSmalltalk: [theAddress].
	self assert: self address = theAddress.
	^theAddress! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
addressOffset
	"Raw field accessor; use address instead."
	^addressOffset! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
addressOffset: anInteger
	"Raw field accessor; use address: instead."
	^addressOffset := anInteger! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'accessing' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
machineCodeBuffer
	"Answer the array into which machine code is generated when concretizing.  In C machineCode
	 shares storage with the operands (see the class comment), which are read while concretizing,
	 so machine code is generated into a separate buffer and copied into machineCode by concretizeAt:."
	<cmacro: '(instruction) (concretizationScratch.machineCode)'>
	^machineCode! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'generate machine code' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
concretizeAt: actualAddress
	"Generate concrete machine code for the instruction at actualAddress,
	 setting machineCodeSize, and answer the following address.
	 In C the machine code is generated into a buffer and then copied into
	 machineCode, which shares storage with the operands; see machineCodeBuffer."

	self address: actualAddress.
	machineCodeSize := self dispatchConcretize.
	self
		cCode: [machineCodeSize > 0 ifTrue: "copy the whole buffer; a constant size copy is faster"
					[objectMemory memcpy: machineCode _: cogit concretizationBuffer _: cogit concretizationBufferSize]]
		inSmalltalk: [self clobberOperandsOverwrittenByMachineCode].
	self assert: (maxSize = nil or: [maxSize >= machineCodeSize]).
	^actualAddress + machineCodeSize! !

!CogAbstractInstruction methodsFor: 'simulation only' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
clobberOperandsOverwrittenByMachineCode
	"In C the operands share storage with the machine code (see the class comment).  Simulate
	 this by invalidating the operands overwritten by the machine code generated, so that any
	 attempt to use them after concretization fails noisily."
	<doNotGenerate>
	0 to: NumOperands - 1 do:
		[:i|
		i * objectMemory wordSize < machineCodeSize ifTrue:
			[operands at: i put: #clobberedByMachineCode]]! !

!CogAbstractInstruction class methodsFor: 'simulation only' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
byteSizeForSimulator: aVMClass
	"Answer an approximation of the byte size of an AbstractInstruction struct.
	 This is for estimating the alloca in allocateOpcodes:bytecodes:ifFail:
	 self allSubclasses collect: [:ea| {ea. ea byteSizeForSimulator: ea basicNew}]"
	| ptrsize |
	ptrsize := self == CogAbstractInstruction ifTrue: [BytesPerWord] ifFalse: [self wordSize].
	^4 "opcode machineCodeSize maxSize annotation"
	+ 4 "addressOffset"
	+ ptrsize "dependent"
	+ (NumOperands * ptrsize max: CogCompilerClass basicNew machineCodeBytes) "operands/machineCode union"
		roundTo: ptrsize! !

!CogAbstractInstruction class methodsFor: 'translation' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
filteredInstVarNames
	"Eliminate bcpc, which is development-time only, and order the fields so that addressOffset
	 follows the byte fields and operands and machineCode, which share storage in C, come last
	 (see printTypedefOn:)."
	^(super filteredInstVarNames copyWithoutAll: #('bcpc' 'addressOffset' 'dependent' 'operands' 'machineCode')),
	   #('addressOffset' 'dependent' 'operands' 'machineCode')! !

!CogAbstractInstruction class methodsFor: 'translation' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
instVarNamesAndTypesForTranslationDo: aBinaryBlock
	"Enumerate aBinaryBlock with the names and C type strings for the inst vars to include in an AbstractInstruction struct."
	"((CogAbstractInstruction withAllSubclasses reject:
		[:c|
		 (c class lookupSelector: #wordSize) isSubclassResponsibility
		 or: [((c lookupSelector: #machineCodeBytes) ifNil: [false] ifNotNil: [:cm| cm isSubclassResponsibility])
		 or: [c name includesSubstring: 'ForTests']]])
			sort: [:a :b| a name <= b name]) do:
			[:c| Transcript cr; cr; print: c; cr. c printTypedefOn: Transcript]"

	"The first four fields of an instruction are byte variables. opcode, machineCodeSize, maxSize, annotation.
	 addressOffset is a 32-bit offset; see the class comment."
	self filteredInstVarNames do:
		[:ivn|
		 aBinaryBlock
			value: ivn
			value: (ivn caseOf: {
						['addressOffset']	-> [#int]. "see Cogit>>codeOffsetForAddress:"
						['machineCode']	-> [self machineCodeDeclaration].
						['operands']		-> [{#usqInt. '[', NumOperands printString, ']'}].
						['dependent']		-> ['struct _AbstractInstruction *']}
					otherwise:
						[#'unsigned char'])]! !

!CogAbstractInstruction class methodsFor: 'translation' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
printTypedefOn: aStream
	"Override to overlay operands and machineCode, which come last (see filteredInstVarNames),
	 in an anonymous union.  Their lifetimes are disjoint; see the class comment."
	| lines index |
	lines := (String streamContents: [:s| super printTypedefOn: s]) lines.
	index := lines findFirst: [:line| line includesSubstring: 'operands['].
	self assert: (index > 0 and: [(lines at: index + 1) includesSubstring: 'machineCode[']).
	lines withIndexDo:
		[:line :i|
		i = index ifTrue:
			[aStream tab; nextPutAll: 'union {'; cr].
		(i = index or: [i = (index + 1)]) ifTrue:
			[aStream tab].
		aStream nextPutAll: line; cr.
		i = (index + 1) ifTrue:
			[aStream tab; nextPutAll: '};'; cr]]! !

!Cogit methodsFor: 'compile abstract instructions' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
codeAddressForOffset: offset
	"In C an instruction's address is held as a 32-bit offset from codeBase, 0 representing no address
	 (see CogAbstractInstruction>>address).  Instructions are always generated within (or, for virtual
	 addresses, near) the code zone; see computeMaximumSizes."
	<cmacro: '(offset) ((offset) ? codeBase - 1 + (sqInt)(offset) : 0)'>
	^offset = 0 ifTrue: [0] ifFalse: [codeBase - 1 + offset]! !

!Cogit methodsFor: 'compile abstract instructions' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
codeOffsetForAddress: address
	"In C an instruction's address is held as a 32-bit offset from codeBase, 0 representing no address
	 (see CogAbstractInstruction>>address:)."
	<cmacro: '(address) ((address) ? (int)((address) - (codeBase - 1)) : 0)'>
	^address = 0 ifTrue: [0] ifFalse: [address - (codeBase - 1)]! !

!Cogit methodsFor: 'compile abstract instructions' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
concretizationBuffer
	"Answer the buffer into which machine code is generated when concretizing; see
	 CogAbstractInstruction>>machineCodeBuffer.  Its element type is that of machineCode."
	<cmacro: '() (concretizationScratch.machineCode)'>
	^self error: 'C only'! !

!Cogit methodsFor: 'compile abstract instructions' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
concretizationBufferSize
	"Answer the byte size of the buffer into which machine code is generated; see concretizationBuffer."
	<cmacro: '() sizeof(concretizationScratch.machineCode)'>
	^self error: 'C only'! !

!Cogit methodsFor: 'generate machine code' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
computeMaximumSizes
	"This pass assigns maximum sizes to all abstract instructions and eliminates jump fixups.
	 It hence assigns the maximum address an instruction will occur at which allows the next
	 pass to conservatively size jumps.  Virtual addresses start at codeBase rather than 0
	 because in C instruction addresses are held as offsets from codeBase (see
	 codeOffsetForAddress:); only differences between virtual addresses matter."
	<inline: false>
	<var: #abstractInstruction type: #'AbstractInstruction *'>
	| relativeAddress |
	literalsManager dumpLiterals: false.
	relativeAddress := self cCode: [codeBase] inSmalltalk: [codeBase ifNil: [0]].
	0 to: opcodeIndex - 1 do:
		[:i| | abstractInstruction |
		self maybeBreakGeneratingInstructionWithIndex: i.
		abstractInstruction := self abstractInstructionAt: i.
		abstractInstruction
			address: relativeAddress;
			maxSize: abstractInstruction computeMaximumSize.
		relativeAddress := relativeAddress + abstractInstruction maxSize]! !

!Cogit class methodsFor: 'translation' stamp: 'cb 10/26/2026 22:30'!
declareCVarsIn: aCCodeGenerator 
	| backEnd |
	backEnd := CogCompilerClass basicNew.
	#('coInterpreter' 'objectMemory' 'methodZone' 'objectRepresentation' 'breakBlock' 'breakPC' 'cogBlockMethodSurrogateClass' 'cogMethodSurrogateClass' 'nsSendCacheSurrogateClass' 'processor' 'processorLock' 'lastNInstructions' 'simulatedAddresses' 'ioHighResClock' 'simulatedTrampolines' 'simulatedVariableGetters' 'simulatedVariableSetters' 'processorFrameValid' 'printRegisters' 'printInstructions' 'clickConfirm' 'clickStepping' 'singleStep' 'codeZoneIsExecutableNotWritable' 'debugAPISelector' 'shortCutTrampolineBlocks' 'debugBytecodePointers' 'debugOpcodeIndices' 'debugInstructionAddress' 'debugInstructionIndices' 'perMethodProfile' 'instructionProfile' 'disassembler')
		do: [:simulationVariableUnusedByRealVM | aCCodeGenerator removeVariable: simulationVariableUnusedByRealVM].
	NewspeakVM
		ifFalse: [#('selfSendTrampolines' 'dynamicSuperSendTrampolines' 'implicitReceiverSendTrampolines' 'outerSendTrampolines' 'ceEnclosingObjectTrampoline' 'numIRCs' 'indexOfIRC' 'theIRCs')
				do: [:variableNotNeededInNormalVM | aCCodeGenerator removeVariable: variableNotNeededInNormalVM]].
	LowcodeVM
		ifFalse: [#('ceMallocTrampoline' 'ceFreeTrampoline' 'ceFFICalloutTrampoline')
				do: [:variableNotNeededInNormalVM | aCCodeGenerator removeVariable: variableNotNeededInNormalVM]].
	aCCodeGenerator removeConstant: #COGMTVM.
	"this should be defined at compile time"
	"N.B. We *do not* include sq.h; it pulls in conflicting definitions now that sqVirtualMachine.h
	declares cointerp's functions, and declares some of them inaccurately for histrical reasons.
	We pull in CoInterpreter's api via cointerp.h which is accurate."
	aCCodeGenerator addHeaderFile: '"sqConfig.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '<stddef.h>';
		 addHeaderFile: '<stdio.h>';
		 addHeaderFile: '<stdlib.h>';
		 addHeaderFile: '<string.h>';
		 addHeaderFile: '"sqPlatformSpecific.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '"sqMemoryAccess.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '"sqCogStackAlignment.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '"dispdbg.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '"cogmethod.h"'.
	"config.h must be first on linux"
	"for e.g. offsetof"
	"e.g. solaris overrides things for sqCogStackAlignment.h"
	"must precede cointerp.h & cogit.h otherwise NoDbgRegParms gets screwed up"
	NewspeakVM
		ifTrue: [aCCodeGenerator addHeaderFile: '"nssendcache.h"'].
	aCCodeGenerator addHeaderFile: '"cointerp.h"';
		 addHeaderFile: '"cogit.h"'.
	aCCodeGenerator var: #ceGetFP declareC: 'usqIntptr_t (*ceGetFP)(void)';
		 var: #ceGetSP declareC: 'usqIntptr_t (*ceGetSP)(void)';
		 var: #ceCaptureCStackPointers declareC: 'void (*ceCaptureCStackPointers)(void)';
		 var: #ceInvokeInterpret declareC: 'void (*ceInvokeInterpret)(void)';
		 var: #ceEnterCogCodePopReceiverReg declareC: 'void (*ceEnterCogCodePopReceiverReg)(void)';
		 var: #realCEEnterCogCodePopReceiverReg declareC: 'void (*realCEEnterCogCodePopReceiverReg)(void)';
		 var: #ceCallCogCodePopReceiverReg declareC: 'void (*ceCallCogCodePopReceiverReg)(void)';
		 var: #realCECallCogCodePopReceiverReg declareC: 'void (*realCECallCogCodePopReceiverReg)(void)';
		 var: #ceCallCogCodePopReceiverAndClassRegs declareC: 'void (*ceCallCogCodePopReceiverAndClassRegs)(void)';
		 var: #realCECallCogCodePopReceiverAndClassRegs declareC: 'void (*realCECallCogCodePopReceiverAndClassRegs)(void)';
		 var: #postCompileHook declareC: 'void (*postCompileHook)(CogMethod *)';
		 var: #openPICList declareC: 'CogMethod *openPICList = 0';
		 var: #maxMethodBefore type: #'CogBlockMethod *';
		 var: 'enumeratingCogMethod' type: #'CogMethod *'.
	aCCodeGenerator var: #ceTryLockVMOwner declareC: '#if COGMTVM\usqIntptr_t (*ceTryLockVMOwner)(usqIntptr_t)\#endif'.
	backEnd numICacheFlushOpcodes > 0
		ifTrue: [aCCodeGenerator var: #ceFlushICache declareC: 'static void (*ceFlushICache)(usqIntptr_t from, usqIntptr_t to)'].
	aCCodeGenerator var: #ceFlushDCache declareC: '#if DUAL_MAPPED_CODE_ZONE\static void (*ceFlushDCache)(usqIntptr_t from, usqIntptr_t to)\#endif';
		 var: #codeToDataDelta declareC: '#if DUAL_MAPPED_CODE_ZONE\static sqInt codeToDataDelta\#else\# define codeToDataDelta 0\#endif';
		 var: #cFramePointerInUse declareC: '#if !!defined(cFramePointerInUse)\sqInt cFramePointerInUse\#endif'.
	aCCodeGenerator declareVar: 'aMethodLabel' type: #AbstractInstruction;
		 var: #backEnd declareC: 'AbstractInstruction * const backEnd = &aMethodLabel';
		 var: #methodLabel declareC: 'AbstractInstruction * const methodLabel = &aMethodLabel'.
	"Has to come lexicographically before backEnd & methodLabel"
	self
		declareC: #(#abstractOpcodes #stackCheckLabel #blockEntryLabel #blockEntryNoContextSwitch #stackOverflowCall #sendMiss #entry #noCheckEntry #selfSendEntry #dynSuperEntry #fullBlockNoContextSwitchEntry #fullBlockEntry #picMNUAbort #picInterpretAbort #endCPICCase0 #endCPICCase1 #cPICEndOfCodeLabel)
		as: #'AbstractInstruction *'
		in: aCCodeGenerator.
	aCCodeGenerator declareVar: #cPICPrototype type: #'CogMethod *';
		 declareVar: #cPICPrototype22 type: #'CogMethod *';
		 declareVar: #blockStarts type: #'BlockStart *';
		 declareVar: #fixups type: #'BytecodeFixup *';
		 declareVar: #codeBase type: #usqInt;
		 declareVar: #methodZoneBase type: #usqInt.
	aCCodeGenerator "machine code buffer; see CogAbstractInstruction>>machineCodeBuffer"
		declareVar: 'concretizationScratch' type: #'AbstractInstruction'.
	aCCodeGenerator var: #ordinarySendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt ordinarySendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]';
		 var: #superSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt superSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]'.
	BytecodeSetHasDirectedSuperSend
		ifTrue: [aCCodeGenerator var: #directedSuperSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt directedSuperSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]';
				 var: #directedSuperBindingSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt directedSuperBindingSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]'].
	NewspeakVM
		ifTrue: [aCCodeGenerator var: #selfSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt selfSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]';
				 var: #dynamicSuperSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt dynamicSuperSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]';
				 var: #implicitReceiverSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt implicitReceiverSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]';
				 var: #outerSendTrampolines declareC: 'sqInt outerSendTrampolines[NumSendTrampolines]'].
	aCCodeGenerator addConstantForBinding: self bindingForNumTrampolines;
		 var: #trampolineAddresses declareC: 'static char *trampolineAddresses[NumTrampolines*2]';
		 var: #objectReferencesInRuntime declareC: 'static usqInt objectReferencesInRuntime[NumObjRefsInRuntime+1]';
		 var: #labelCounter type: #int;
		 var: #traceFlags declareC: 'int traceFlags = 8 /* prim trace log on by default */';
		 declareVar: #traceFlagsMeanings type: #'const char *';
		
		var: #traceFlagsMeanings
		declareC: (CCodeGenerator new
				arrayInitializerCalled: #traceFlagsMeanings
				for: (Cogit basicNew sendTrace: -1)
				sizeString: nil
				type: #'const char *');
		 var: #cStackAlignment declareC: 'const int cStackAlignment = STACK_ALIGN_BYTES & STACK_ALIGN_MASK'.
	aCCodeGenerator declareVar: #minValidCallAddress type: #'usqIntptr_t'.
	aCCodeGenerator vmClass generatorTable
		ifNotNil: [:bytecodeGenTable | aCCodeGenerator var: #generatorTable declareC: 'static BytecodeDescriptor generatorTable[' , bytecodeGenTable size printString , ']'
					, (self tableInitializerFor: bytecodeGenTable in: aCCodeGenerator)].
	"In C the abstract opcode names clash with the Smalltalk generator syntactic sugar.
	Most of the syntactic sugar is inlined, but alas some remains.  Rename the syntactic
	sugar to avoid the clash."
	(self organization listAtCategoryNamed: #'abstract instructions')
		do: [:s | aCCodeGenerator addSelectorTranslation: s to: 'g'
					, (aCCodeGenerator cFunctionNameFor: s)].
	(self organization listAtCategoryNamed: #'generate machine code - dual mapped zone support')
		do: [:s | (s endsWith: 'At:put:')
				ifTrue: [aCCodeGenerator addKernelAtPutTranslationFor: s]].
	aCCodeGenerator addSelectorTranslation: #halt: to: 'haltmsg'.
	self declareFlagVarsAsByteIn: aCCodeGenerator! !

